<DocsLayout title="Private Barcode Vault & Product Workspace | BarcodeNest" description="Save private barcode and product records, organize collections, export data and print labels. Understand Vault storage capacities and account access." heading="A home for your product records." intro="Save the work once. Reopen your products without spending another lookup credit." current="vault">
<section><h2>Save and organize private products</h2><p>Open <a href="/vault/">My Barcode Vault</a> to add a product or edit an existing record. Store an identifier, name, SKU, brand, category, collection, notes, an HTTPS image link and up to 20 custom fields. Prices are optional and support USD, EUR and GBP. Scanner results and generated barcodes have a Save to Vault action. Saving is explicit; ordinary API lookups are not automatically added to your Vault.</p><p>Vault records belong to the signed-in account. They are separate from the public product catalog, and private entries are not published or shared with other accounts. Image fields store links, not uploaded image files. A record may describe an internal item that has no public lookup match.</p></section>
<section><h2>Storage capacity and plan changes</h2><p>Free and One-time have capacity for 25 records, Creator 250, Starter 2,000 and Growth 10,000. This is persistent storage capacity, not a monthly counter. Removing a record frees a slot. If a downgrade leaves you above capacity, your records remain readable, editable and removable; adding another record requires freeing capacity or upgrading. CSV and JSON exports are included in Creator, Starter and Growth.</p><p>Saving the same identifier again returns the existing record and preserves your edits. Equivalent retail GTIN representations share one saved record. Barcode generation, product lookup, scanning and labels keep their separate allowances.</p></section>
<section><h2>Reopen, refresh or print</h2><p>Reading and editing saved records uses no product lookup credits. Look up product details is an explicit request using the existing lookup rules; review its result before saving it. Creator has no product lookup units, but can save manually entered records and scanned identifiers.</p><p>Select products in the Vault to create an A4 PDF, one label per selected record. This uses label units. Label output supports EAN-13, UPC-A, Code 128 and QR. Other stored formats remain available for organization and export. Generating a new image also uses generation units; the Vault stores its underlying identifier rather than retaining the generated image file.</p></section>
<section><h2>Account API</h2><p>Vault endpoints use the account session or its bearer access token, rather than a barcode API key. Browser cookie requests must originate from an allowed website origin. List records with <code>GET /v1/account/vault</code>; optional parameters are <code>q</code>, <code>collection</code>, <code>offset</code> and <code>limit</code> (maximum 100). The response includes items, matching total, collections, current storage used and capacity.</p><p>Create a record with <code>POST /v1/account/vault</code> and a JSON body:</p><CodeBlock label="Private product record" language="json" code={example} /><p>The response includes <code>item</code> and <code>created</code>. Repeated saves do not overwrite an existing record. Get or delete a record at <code>/v1/account/vault/ID</code>. To edit, send a full record body with <code>PUT</code> and include its current <code>revision</code>. A stale revision returns 409 so another edit cannot be overwritten silently.</p><p>Paid exports use <code>GET /v1/account/vault/export?format=csv</code> or <code>format=json</code>, with an optional collection. Exports are limited to 10,000 records. CSV prices use integer minor units, so 1299 means USD 12.99. Import barcode columns into Excel as Text to preserve leading zeros; potentially executable spreadsheet cells are escaped. An Excel workbook format is not included.</p></section>
<section><h2>Errors</h2><p>A full Vault returns 409 with <code>vault_capacity_reached</code>. Stale edits return <code>vault_edit_conflict</code>; changing a record to an already saved identifier returns <code>vault_duplicate</code>. Unknown records, including IDs belonging to another account, return 404. Invalid fields return 422 and exports excluded from your plan return 403. Your data is not deleted by a capacity error.</p></section>
</DocsLayout>
